WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.233
Claude Code in one terminal.

2
00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:03.300
Codex in another.

3
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.633
And you in the middle,

4
00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:07.333
copying context between them all day.

5
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.867
You paste the goal,

6
00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:11.167
the error, what the other agent decided.

7
00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.567
The agents write the code.

8
00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.033
You do the routing.

9
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.600
SpecWithCode is a free Mac app for the

10
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.033
coding agents you already pay for:

11
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.933
Claude Code, Codex,

12
00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:22.733
Grok Build, Cursor,

13
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:25.600
OpenCode, Copilot, Antigravity and Pi.

14
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.767
It takes the routing off your hands.

15
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.533
Add a project over a real folder.

16
00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:32.033
It gets one coordinator:

17
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.533
a conversation that routes and tracks the work,

18
00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:37.033
while worker threads write the code.

19
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.267
Describe the work once.

20
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:41.267
Quick questions it answers itself.

21
00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.767
Code changes, long research and tool work go

22
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.433
to worker threads it starts.

23
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.700
Here it started two workers:

24
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.567
Claude on the greeting,

25
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:52.067
and Codex on the CI workflow,

26
00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.733
because the ask named Codex.

27
00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:57.100
Each one gets a card and a link.

28
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.467
Follow-ups go to the worker already on that

29
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.733
area, so nothing is assigned twice.

30
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:04.367
When a worker finishes,

31
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.333
its report comes back on its own.

32
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:08.200
No polling, no pasting.

33
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.633
The coordinator and the workers have separate models.

34
00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:15.067
Keep the coordinator on Claude Opus 5.5,

35
00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.933
set a default worker model,

36
00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:18.600
or name one in the ask,

37
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.000
like Codex here.

38
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.000
The usage chip shows one ring per subscription,

39
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.367
amber at 80 percent,

40
00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.167
red at 95.

41
00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.467
If one runs out,

42
00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:32.267
the thread offers to continue on another signed-in provider.

43
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.233
For bigger work,

44
00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:35.900
the Plan holds a short spec,

45
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.733
acceptance criteria and tasks,

46
00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:39.067
and who owns each.

47
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.867
A worker can report a task done.

48
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.333
Only you make it Verified:

49
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:46.500
Run verification runs its check and keeps a receipt.

50
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.900
The agents write the code.

51
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.333
The coordinator routes it.

52
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.800
You review the results.

53
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.833
SpecWithCode is free,

54
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:54.633
with no account,

55
00:01:54.633 --> 00:01:56.167
for Apple silicon Macs.

56
00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.067
Get it at spec-weave.com/studio.
